# The pre-commit hook is a POSIX shell script executed by Git Bash's `sh`. On Windows,
# git's global core.autocrlf=true would otherwise convert its LF line endings to CRLF on
# checkout, which can break `sh` parsing (a stray \r after `set -e` / `if ! cmd; then`).
# Force LF regardless of the checkout machine's autocrlf setting.
.githooks/pre-commit text eol=lf
